				"question": "What are governance tokens?",
				"answer": "Governance tokens give holders voting rights in a protocol's decisions. Examples: UNI (Uniswap), AAVE, COMP. Voting power typically scales with token holdings."
			},
			{
				"question": "How does vote delegation work?",
				"answer": "You can delegate your voting power to others (delegates) while keeping your tokens. This helps active community members vote on behalf of passive holders."
			},
			{
				"question": "Do governance tokens have value?",
				"answer": "Value comes from governance rights, potential fee sharing, and speculation. Some protocols share revenue with token holders. Others have struggled to accrue value."
			}
		]
